[patterns/information/api-microservices/PTN-INF-API-001-data-consistency-pattern.md#6-reconciliation-and-data-quality-monitoring]

#### 6. Reconciliation and Data Quality Monitoring

**Purpose**: Detect and resolve inconsistencies between services. Eventual consistency means services temporarily inconsistent; reconciliation ensures convergence to consistent state.

**Reconciliation Strategies**:

**A. Scheduled Reconciliation (Batch)**

Periodic jobs compare data across services, detect discrepancies, trigger remediation.

```javascript
// Nightly reconciliation job (runs at 2 AM)
async function reconcileMemberEligibility() {
    console.log('Starting member eligibility reconciliation...');

    // Query all active members from Member Service (source of truth)
    const activeMembers = await memberService.getActiveMembers();
    console.log(`Found ${activeMembers.length} active members`);

    // Query member eligibility cache in Claims Service
    const eligibilityCache = await claimsService.getEligibilityCache();

    // Compare and detect discrepancies
    const discrepancies = [];

    for (const member of activeMembers) {
        const cached = eligibilityCache.find(c => c.memberId === member.id);

        if (!cached) {
            // Missing from cache: should be eligible but not in Claims Service
            discrepancies.push({
                type: 'missing',
                memberId: member.id,
                expected: 'eligible',
                actual: 'not found'
            });
        } else if (cached.enrollmentDate !== member.enrollmentDate) {
            // Enrollment date mismatch
            discrepancies.push({
                type: 'mismatch',
                memberId: member.id,
                field: 'enrollmentDate',
                expected: member.enrollmentDate,
                actual: cached.enrollmentDate
            });
        }
    }

    // Check for terminated members still in cache
    for (const cached of eligibilityCache) {
        const member = activeMembers.find(m => m.id === cached.memberId);
        if (!member) {
            discrepancies.push({
                type: 'orphan',
                memberId: cached.memberId,
                expected: 'not in cache',
                actual: 'still cached'
            });
        }
    }

    console.log(`Found ${discrepancies.length} discrepancies`);

    // Remediate discrepancies
    for (const discrepancy of discrepancies) {
        switch (discrepancy.type) {
            case 'missing':
                // Re-publish enrollment event to populate cache
                await eventBus.publish('member.enrolled.reconciliation', {
                    memberId: discrepancy.memberId,
                    reason: 'reconciliation'
                });
                break;
            case 'orphan':
                // Remove from cache (member terminated)
                await claimsService.removeFromCache(discrepancy.memberId);
                break;
            case 'mismatch':
                // Update cache with correct value
                await claimsService.updateCache(discrepancy.memberId, {
                    [discrepancy.field]: discrepancy.expected
                });
                break;
        }
    }

    // Generate reconciliation report
    await reportingService.createReconciliationReport({
        timestamp: new Date(),
        totalMembers: activeMembers.length,
        discrepancies: discrepancies.length,
        discrepancyRate: (discrepancies.length / activeMembers.length * 100).toFixed(2) + '%',
        details: discrepancies
    });
}
```

**B. Real-Time Reconciliation (Continuous)**

Monitor data quality metrics continuously; alert when metrics exceed thresholds.

```javascript
// Real-time data quality monitoring
setInterval(async () => {
    // Check event bus lag (how far behind are consumers?)
    const lag = await eventBus.getConsumerLag('claims-service');
    if (lag.messagesBacklog > 100000) {
        await alertService.notify({
            severity: 'high',
            message: 'Claims Service consumer lag exceeds threshold',
            details: { backlog: lag.messagesBacklog, latency: lag.lagSeconds }
        });
    }

    // Check reconciliation metrics
    const metrics = await reconciliationService.getMetrics();
    if (metrics.discrepancyRate > 0.5) { // >0.5% discrepancy rate
        await alertService.notify({
            severity: 'medium',
            message: 'Data consistency discrepancy rate high',
            details: { rate: metrics.discrepancyRate, count: metrics.discrepancyCount }
        });
    }
}, 60000); // Check every minute
```

**C. Merkle Tree Reconciliation** (Efficient Comparison)

Compare large datasets efficiently using hash trees. Detect which portions of dataset differ without comparing every record.

**How It Works**:
1. Divide dataset into chunks (e.g., 1000 records per chunk)
2. Compute hash of each chunk
3. Build tree of hashes (parent hash = hash of child hashes)
4. Compare root hashes; if different, recursively compare child hashes to find differing chunks
5. Only retrieve and compare records in differing chunks

**Benefits**: Compare millions of records efficiently; only transfer/compare records that actually differ.

**Data Quality Metrics** (Prometheus):

```yaml
# Consistency lag (how long until services converge)
consistency_lag_seconds{service="claims-service"} 2.5

# Discrepancy rate (% of records inconsistent)
consistency_discrepancy_rate{service_pair="member-to-claims"} 0.0023

# Reconciliation success rate
reconciliation_success_rate{job="nightly-reconciliation"} 0.9987

# Dead letter queue depth (failed messages)
dead_letter_queue_depth{queue="member.enrolled.dlq"} 3
```

