[patterns/information/api-microservices/PTN-INF-API-001-data-consistency-pattern.md#example-1-member-enrollment-saga-choreography-based]

### Example 1: Member Enrollment Saga (Choreography-Based)

**Business Context**:

When member enrolls in Medicaid program via online portal, enrollment spans multiple services:

1. Member Service creates member record
2. Eligibility Service creates eligibility determination
3. Claims Service enables claims processing
4. Provider Network Service assigns primary care provider (PCP)
5. Card Printing Service queues ID card printing
6. Notification Service sends welcome email

Traditional approach would require distributed transaction coordinating all 6 services. Data Consistency Pattern uses choreography-based saga with eventual consistency.

**Architecture**:

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant Portal as Member Portal
    participant MS as Member Service
    participant EB as Event Bus
    participant ES as Eligibility Service
    participant CS as Claims Service
    participant PN as Provider Network
    participant CP as Card Printing
    participant NS as Notification Service

    Portal->>MS: POST /api/members/enroll
    MS->>MS: Validate & Create Member<br/>(Local TX)
    MS->>MS: Write to Outbox<br/>(Same TX)
    MS-->>Portal: 202 Accepted<br/>{memberId, status: "enrolling"}

    MS->>EB: Publish: member.enrolled

    EB->>ES: Event: member.enrolled
    ES->>ES: Create Eligibility<br/>(Local TX)
    ES->>EB: Publish: eligibility.created

    EB->>CS: Event: eligibility.created
    CS->>CS: Enable Claims<br/>(Local TX)
    CS->>EB: Publish: claims.enabled

    EB->>PN: Event: member.enrolled
    PN->>PN: Assign PCP<br/>(Local TX)
    PN->>EB: Publish: pcp.assigned

    EB->>CP: Event: member.enrolled
    CP->>CP: Queue Card Printing<br/>(Local TX)
    CP->>EB: Publish: card.queued

    EB->>NS: Event: member.enrolled
    NS->>NS: Send Welcome Email
    NS->>EB: Publish: welcome.email.sent
```

**Implementation**:

**Member Service** (Event Publisher):

```javascript
// Member Service: Enroll member and publish event
const express = require('express');
const { v4: uuidv4 } = require('uuid');
const { ServiceBusClient } = require('@azure/service-bus');

const app = express();
const serviceBusClient = new ServiceBusClient(connectionString);
const sender = serviceBusClient.createSender('member-events');

app.post('/api/members/enroll', async (req, res) => {
    const { firstName, lastName, dateOfBirth, ssn, address, email } = req.body;
    const correlationId = req.headers['x-correlation-id'] || uuidv4();

    try {
        // Start database transaction
        const transaction = await db.transaction();

        try {
            // Step 1: Create member record
            const memberId = uuidv4();
            const member = {
                id: memberId,
                firstName,
                lastName,
                dateOfBirth,
                ssn,
                address,
                email,
                enrollmentDate: new Date(),
                status: 'enrolling',
                version: 1
            };

            await db.members.insert(member, { transaction });

            // Step 2: Write event to outbox (same transaction)
            const outboxEvent = {
                eventId: uuidv4(),
                aggregateId: memberId,
                aggregateType: 'Member',
                eventType: 'member.enrolled',
                eventPayload: JSON.stringify({
                    eventId: uuidv4(),
                    eventType: 'member.enrolled',
                    eventVersion: '1.0',
                    timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),
                    source: 'member-service',
                    correlationId: correlationId,
                    data: {
                        memberId,
                        firstName,
                        lastName,
                        dateOfBirth,
                        ssn,
                        enrollmentDate: new Date().toISOString(),
                        address,
                        email
                    }
                }),
                correlationId,
                status: 'Pending',
                createdAt: new Date()
            };

            await db.outbox.insert(outboxEvent, { transaction });

            // Commit transaction (atomically persists member and event)
            await transaction.commit();

            console.log(`Member enrolled: ${memberId}, CorrelationId: ${correlationId}`);

            // Return 202 Accepted (enrollment in progress)
            res.status(202).json({
                memberId,
                status: 'enrolling',
                message: 'Enrollment initiated. You will receive confirmation email shortly.',
                correlationId
            });

        } catch (error) {
            await transaction.rollback();
            throw error;
        }

    } catch (error) {
        console.error('Member enrollment failed:', error);
        res.status(500).json({ error: 'Enrollment failed', details: error.message });
    }
});

// Outbox publisher (background job)
setInterval(async () => {
    try {
        // Fetch pending outbox events
        const pendingEvents = await db.outbox.findAll({
            where: { status: 'Pending' },
            order: [['createdAt', 'ASC']],
            limit: 100
        });

        for (const outboxEvent of pendingEvents) {
            try {
                // Publish to Azure Service Bus
                const message = {
                    body: outboxEvent.eventPayload,
                    messageId: outboxEvent.eventId,
                    correlationId: outboxEvent.correlationId,
                    contentType: 'application/json',
                    subject: 'member.enrolled'
                };

                await sender.sendMessages(message);

                // Mark as published
                await db.outbox.update(
                    { status: 'Published', processedAt: new Date() },
                    { where: { eventId: outboxEvent.eventId } }
                );

                console.log(`Published outbox event: ${outboxEvent.eventId}`);

            } catch (error) {
                // Increment retry count
                await db.outbox.update(
                    {
                        retryCount: db.sequelize.literal('retryCount + 1'),
                        lastError: error.message
                    },
                    { where: { eventId: outboxEvent.eventId } }
                );

                console.error(`Failed to publish outbox event: ${outboxEvent.eventId}`, error);
            }
        }
    } catch (error) {
        console.error('Outbox publisher error:', error);
    }
}, 5000); // Run every 5 seconds

app.listen(3000, () => console.log('Member Service listening on port 3000'));
```

**Claims Service** (Event Subscriber):

```javascript
// Claims Service: Subscribe to member.enrolled events
const { ServiceBusClient } = require('@azure/service-bus');
const redis = require('redis');

const serviceBusClient = new ServiceBusClient(connectionString);
const receiver = serviceBusClient.createReceiver('member-events', 'claims-service-subscription');
const redisClient = redis.createClient();
const processedMessages = redisClient.duplicate(); // Idempotency store

// Message handler
receiver.subscribe({
    processMessage: async (message) => {
        const messageId = message.messageId;
        const correlationId = message.correlationId;

        console.log(`Processing message: ${messageId}, Correlation: ${correlationId}`);

        try {
            // Check idempotency (detect duplicate messages)
            const alreadyProcessed = await processedMessages.get(`processed:${messageId}`);
            if (alreadyProcessed) {
                console.log(`Duplicate message detected: ${messageId}, skipping...`);
                await receiver.completeMessage(message);
                return;
            }

            // Parse event
            const event = JSON.parse(message.body);

            // Update local member cache for eligibility checks
            await db.memberCache.upsert({
                memberId: event.data.memberId,
                firstName: event.data.firstName,
                lastName: event.data.lastName,
                dateOfBirth: event.data.dateOfBirth,
                eligible: true,
                effectiveDate: event.data.enrollmentDate,
                lastUpdated: new Date(),
                version: 1
            });

            // Record message as processed (24-hour TTL)
            await processedMessages.setEx(`processed:${messageId}`, 86400, JSON.stringify({
                processedAt: new Date().toISOString(),
                correlationId: correlationId
            }));

            console.log(`Successfully processed member.enrolled: ${event.data.memberId}`);

            // Acknowledge message
            await receiver.completeMessage(message);

            // Publish domain event: claims enabled
            await eventPublisher.publish({
                eventType: 'claims.enabled',
                eventVersion: '1.0',
                timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),
                source: 'claims-service',
                correlationId: correlationId,
                data: {
                    memberId: event.data.memberId,
                    enabledAt: new Date().toISOString()
                }
            });

        } catch (error) {
            console.error(`Error processing message: ${error}`);

            // Reject message (will be redelivered or moved to DLQ after max retries)
            await receiver.abandonMessage(message);
        }
    },

    processError: async (error) => {
        console.error(`Subscription error: ${error}`);

        // Alert operations team
        await alertService.notify({
            severity: 'high',
            message: 'Claims Service event subscription error',
            details: { error: error.message, timestamp: new Date() }
        });
    }
});

console.log('Claims Service event consumer started');
```

**Success Scenario** (End-to-End Timeline):

```text
T+0ms:    Member submits enrollment via portal
T+50ms:   Member Service persists member + outbox event (local TX)
T+50ms:   Member Service returns 202 Accepted to portal
T+100ms:  Portal shows "Enrollment in progress..." message
T+5.1s:   Outbox publisher publishes member.enrolled event to Azure Service Bus
T+5.15s:  Eligibility Service receives event, creates eligibility record
T+5.2s:   Eligibility Service publishes eligibility.created event
T+5.25s:  Claims Service receives eligibility.created event, enables claims processing
T+5.3s:   Claims Service publishes claims.enabled event
T+5.35s:  Provider Network Service receives member.enrolled event, assigns PCP
T+5.4s:   Provider Network Service publishes pcp.assigned event
T+5.45s:  Card Printing Service receives member.enrolled event, queues card printing
T+5.5s:   Card Printing Service publishes card.queued event
T+5.55s:  Notification Service receives member.enrolled event, sends welcome email
T+6s:     Notification Service publishes welcome.email.sent event
T+6s:     Member receives welcome email: "Enrollment complete! Your member ID is..."

Total Duration: 6 seconds (member enrolled and operational across all services)
```

**Failure Scenario: Claims Service Unavailable**

```text
T+0ms:    Member submits enrollment
T+50ms:   Member Service persists member + outbox event, returns 202 Accepted
T+5.1s:   Outbox publisher publishes member.enrolled event
T+5.15s:  Eligibility Service processes event successfully
T+5.2s:   Claims Service UNAVAILABLE (pod crashed)
T+5.2s:   Azure Service Bus queues message for Claims Service (not delivered due to no active receiver)
T+10min:  Operations team alerted: "Claims Service consumers offline"
T+12min:  Kubernetes detects pod crash, restarts pod
T+12.5min: Claims Service consumer starts, connects to Azure Service Bus
T+12.6min: Claims Service receives queued member.enrolled event (delivered after recovery)
T+12.7min: Claims Service processes event, enables claims processing
T+12.8min: System consistent across all services (eventual consistency after 12-minute delay)

Total Duration: 12 minutes (delayed due to service outage, but no data loss)
```

**Benefits Demonstrated**:

1. **High Availability**: Member Service remained available despite Claims Service outage; enrollment succeeded
2. **Fault Tolerance**: Claims Service automatically caught up after recovery; no manual intervention required
3. **Loose Coupling**: Services don't know about each other; only know event schemas
4. **Scalability**: Each service can scale independently based on load

