### Example 2: Claims Processing Saga (Orchestration-Based)

**Business Context**:

Claims processing requires strict ordering and complex business logic:

1. Validate claim format (EDI 837, FHIR Claim)
2. Verify member eligibility
3. Validate provider credentials
4. Check prior authorization
5. Apply state-specific adjudication rules
6. Calculate payment
7. Generate remittance advice
8. Update reporting

Failure at any step requires compensating previous steps. Orchestration-based saga provides centralized control for complex workflow.

**Architecture**:

```mermaid
graph TB
    subgraph "Claims Orchestrator"
        Orch[Orchestrator Service]
        SagaDB[(Saga State DB)]
    end

    subgraph "Participant Services"
        Validate[Claims Validation Service]
        Eligibility[Eligibility Service]
        Provider[Provider Service]
        Auth[Prior Auth Service]
        Adjudicate[Adjudication Engine]
        Payment[Payment Service]
        Reporting[Reporting Service]
    end

    Orch -->|1. Validate| Validate
    Orch -->|2. Check Eligibility| Eligibility
    Orch -->|3. Validate Provider| Provider
    Orch -->|4. Check Auth| Auth
    Orch -->|5. Adjudicate| Adjudicate
    Orch -->|6. Process Payment| Payment
    Orch -->|7. Update Reporting| Reporting
    Orch --> SagaDB

    style Orch fill:#ff9999
    style SagaDB fill:#99ccff
```

**Implementation**:

**Saga Orchestrator**:

```csharp
// Claims Processing Saga Orchestrator
public class ClaimsProcessingSaga {
    private readonly IClaimsValidationService _validationService;
    private readonly IEligibilityService _eligibilityService;
    private readonly IProviderService _providerService;
    private readonly IPriorAuthService _priorAuthService;
    private readonly IAdjudicationEngine _adjudicationEngine;
    private readonly IPaymentService _paymentService;
    private readonly IReportingService _reportingService;
    private readonly ISagaRepository _sagaRepository;
    private readonly ILogger<ClaimsProcessingSaga> _logger;

    public async Task<SagaResult> ExecuteAsync(ClaimsProcessingRequest request) {
        var sagaId = Guid.NewGuid();
        var correlationId = Activity.Current?.Id ?? Guid.NewGuid().ToString();

        // Initialize saga state
        var saga = new SagaInstance {
            SagaId = sagaId,
            SagaType = "claims-processing",
            Status = "Running",
            StartedAt = DateTime.UtcNow,
            CorrelationId = correlationId,
            Data = JsonSerializer.Serialize(request)
        };
        await _sagaRepository.CreateAsync(saga);

        var completedSteps = new List<SagaStepResult>();

        try {
            // Step 1: Validate claim format
            _logger.LogInformation("Saga {SagaId}: Step 1 - Validate claim", sagaId);
            await RecordStepAsync(sagaId, "validate-claim", "Started");

            var validationResult = await _validationService.ValidateClaimAsync(request.ClaimData);
            if (!validationResult.IsValid) {
                throw new ValidationException($"Claim validation failed: {validationResult.Errors}");
            }

            await RecordStepAsync(sagaId, "validate-claim", "Completed");
            completedSteps.Add(new SagaStepResult { StepName = "validate-claim", Data = validationResult });

            // Step 2: Verify member eligibility
            _logger.LogInformation("Saga {SagaId}: Step 2 - Check eligibility", sagaId);
            await RecordStepAsync(sagaId, "check-eligibility", "Started");

            var eligibilityResult = await _eligibilityService.CheckEligibilityAsync(
                request.MemberId,
                request.ServiceDate
            );
            if (!eligibilityResult.IsEligible) {
                throw new BusinessRuleException($"Member not eligible: {eligibilityResult.Reason}");
            }

            await RecordStepAsync(sagaId, "check-eligibility", "Completed", eligibilityResult);
            completedSteps.Add(new SagaStepResult { StepName = "check-eligibility", Data = eligibilityResult });

            // Step 3: Validate provider credentials
            _logger.LogInformation("Saga {SagaId}: Step 3 - Validate provider", sagaId);
            await RecordStepAsync(sagaId, "validate-provider", "Started");

            var providerResult = await _providerService.ValidateProviderAsync(
                request.ProviderId,
                request.ServiceDate
            );
            if (!providerResult.IsValid) {
                throw new BusinessRuleException($"Provider invalid: {providerResult.Reason}");
            }

            await RecordStepAsync(sagaId, "validate-provider", "Completed", providerResult);
            completedSteps.Add(new SagaStepResult { StepName = "validate-provider", Data = providerResult });

            // Step 4: Check prior authorization
            _logger.LogInformation("Saga {SagaId}: Step 4 - Check prior authorization", sagaId);
            await RecordStepAsync(sagaId, "check-prior-auth", "Started");

            var authResult = await _priorAuthService.CheckAuthorizationAsync(
                request.MemberId,
                request.ProcedureCode,
                request.ServiceDate
            );
            if (authResult.RequiresAuth && !authResult.IsAuthorized) {
                throw new BusinessRuleException($"Prior authorization required but not found");
            }

            await RecordStepAsync(sagaId, "check-prior-auth", "Completed", authResult);
            completedSteps.Add(new SagaStepResult { StepName = "check-prior-auth", Data = authResult });

            // Step 5: Adjudicate claim (apply pricing rules)
            _logger.LogInformation("Saga {SagaId}: Step 5 - Adjudicate claim", sagaId);
            await RecordStepAsync(sagaId, "adjudicate-claim", "Started");

            var adjudicationResult = await _adjudicationEngine.AdjudicateAsync(new AdjudicationRequest {
                ClaimId = request.ClaimId,
                MemberId = request.MemberId,
                ProviderId = request.ProviderId,
                ProcedureCode = request.ProcedureCode,
                BilledAmount = request.BilledAmount,
                ServiceDate = request.ServiceDate,
                StateContractId = request.StateContractId
            });

            await RecordStepAsync(sagaId, "adjudicate-claim", "Completed", adjudicationResult);
            completedSteps.Add(new SagaStepResult {
                StepName = "adjudicate-claim",
                Data = adjudicationResult,
                RequiresCompensation = true // Claims adjudication is reversible
            });

            // Step 6: Process payment
            _logger.LogInformation("Saga {SagaId}: Step 6 - Process payment", sagaId);
            await RecordStepAsync(sagaId, "process-payment", "Started");

            var paymentResult = await _paymentService.ProcessPaymentAsync(new PaymentRequest {
                ClaimId = request.ClaimId,
                ProviderId = request.ProviderId,
                Amount = adjudicationResult.AllowedAmount,
                PaymentDate = DateTime.UtcNow.AddDays(14) // Standard payment terms
            });

            await RecordStepAsync(sagaId, "process-payment", "Completed", paymentResult);
            completedSteps.Add(new SagaStepResult {
                StepName = "process-payment",
                Data = paymentResult,
                RequiresCompensation = true // Payment is reversible
            });

            // Step 7: Update reporting
            _logger.LogInformation("Saga {SagaId}: Step 7 - Update reporting", sagaId);
            await RecordStepAsync(sagaId, "update-reporting", "Started");

            await _reportingService.RecordClaimAsync(new ClaimReportingData {
                ClaimId = request.ClaimId,
                MemberId = request.MemberId,
                ProviderId = request.ProviderId,
                ServiceDate = request.ServiceDate,
                BilledAmount = request.BilledAmount,
                AllowedAmount = adjudicationResult.AllowedAmount,
                AdjudicationDate = DateTime.UtcNow,
                PaymentAmount = paymentResult.Amount,
                PaymentDate = paymentResult.PaymentDate
            });

            await RecordStepAsync(sagaId, "update-reporting", "Completed");
            completedSteps.Add(new SagaStepResult { StepName = "update-reporting" });

            // Saga completed successfully
            await _sagaRepository.MarkAsCompletedAsync(sagaId);

            _logger.LogInformation(
                "Saga {SagaId} completed successfully: Claim {ClaimId}, Allowed ${Amount}",
                sagaId, request.ClaimId, adjudicationResult.AllowedAmount
            );

            return new SagaResult {
                SagaId = sagaId,
                Status = "Completed",
                ClaimId = request.ClaimId,
                AdjudicationResult = adjudicationResult,
                PaymentResult = paymentResult
            };

        } catch (Exception ex) {
            _logger.LogError(ex, "Saga {SagaId} failed: {Error}", sagaId, ex.Message);

            // Saga failed: compensate completed steps
            await CompensateAsync(sagaId, completedSteps, request);

            return new SagaResult {
                SagaId = sagaId,
                Status = "Failed",
                Error = ex.Message,
                ClaimId = request.ClaimId
            };
        }
    }

    private async Task CompensateAsync(
        Guid sagaId,
        List<SagaStepResult> completedSteps,
        ClaimsProcessingRequest request
    ) {
        await _sagaRepository.MarkAsCompensatingAsync(sagaId);

        _logger.LogWarning("Saga {SagaId}: Starting compensation", sagaId);

        // Compensate in reverse order (LIFO)
        completedSteps.Reverse();

        foreach (var step in completedSteps.Where(s => s.RequiresCompensation)) {
            try {
                await RecordStepAsync(sagaId, step.StepName, "Compensating");

                switch (step.StepName) {
                    case "adjudicate-claim":
                        // Reverse claim adjudication (mark as denied)
                        await _adjudicationEngine.ReverseAdjudicationAsync(request.ClaimId);
                        _logger.LogInformation("Saga {SagaId}: Reversed adjudication", sagaId);
                        break;

                    case "process-payment":
                        // Reverse payment (issue credit)
                        var paymentData = (PaymentResult)step.Data;
                        await _paymentService.ReversePaymentAsync(paymentData.PaymentId);
                        _logger.LogInformation("Saga {SagaId}: Reversed payment {PaymentId}", sagaId, paymentData.PaymentId);
                        break;
                }

                await RecordStepAsync(sagaId, step.StepName, "Compensated");

            } catch (Exception ex) {
                _logger.LogError(ex, "Saga {SagaId}: Compensation failed for step {Step}", sagaId, step.StepName);

                await RecordStepAsync(sagaId, step.StepName, "Compensation Failed", new { error = ex.Message });

                // Alert operations team for manual intervention
                await AlertOperationsAsync(new CompensationAlert {
                    Severity = "critical",
                    SagaId = sagaId,
                    StepName = step.StepName,
                    Error = ex.Message,
                    ClaimId = request.ClaimId,
                    ManualActionRequired = "Review saga state and manually reverse step if needed"
                });
            }
        }

        await _sagaRepository.MarkAsCompensatedAsync(sagaId);

        _logger.LogWarning("Saga {SagaId}: Compensation completed", sagaId);
    }

    private async Task RecordStepAsync(Guid sagaId, string stepName, string status, object data = null) {
        await _sagaRepository.RecordStepAsync(new SagaStep {
            StepId = Guid.NewGuid(),
            SagaId = sagaId,
            StepName = stepName,
            Status = status,
            Timestamp = DateTime.UtcNow,
            Data = data != null ? JsonSerializer.Serialize(data) : null
        });
    }
}
```

**Compensation Example: Prior Authorization Check Fails**

```text
T+0ms:     Saga starts
T+50ms:    Step 1 (validate-claim): Success
T+100ms:   Step 2 (check-eligibility): Success
T+150ms:   Step 3 (validate-provider): Success
T+200ms:   Step 4 (check-prior-auth): FAIL - Prior authorization required but not found
T+250ms:   Saga initiates compensation (reverse order)
T+250ms:   Compensate Step 3 (validate-provider): No compensation needed (read-only operation)
T+250ms:   Compensate Step 2 (check-eligibility): No compensation needed (read-only operation)
T+250ms:   Compensate Step 1 (validate-claim): No compensation needed (read-only operation)
T+300ms:   Saga marked as "Compensated"
T+300ms:   Claim marked as "Denied - Prior Authorization Required"

Result: Claim denied; no side effects; system consistent
```

**Compensation Example: Payment Processing Fails After Adjudication**

```text
T+0ms:     Saga starts
T+50ms:    Step 1-4: All succeed
T+300ms:   Step 6 (process-payment): FAIL - Payment Service timeout
T+350ms:   Saga initiates compensation
T+350ms:   Compensate Step 5 (adjudicate-claim): Reverse adjudication (mark claim as "Adjudication Reversed")
T+400ms:   Compensation complete
T+400ms:   Saga marked as "Compensated"
T+400ms:   Alert sent to operations team: "Claim adjudicated but payment failed; adjudication reversed"

Result: Claim adjudication reversed; no payment issued; system consistent
```

**Monitoring**:

```yaml
# Saga duration histogram
claims_saga_duration_seconds_bucket{saga_type="claims-processing",le="1"} 8500   # 85% complete in <1s
claims_saga_duration_seconds_bucket{saga_type="claims-processing",le="2"} 9500   # 95% complete in <2s
claims_saga_duration_seconds_bucket{saga_type="claims-processing",le="5"} 9900   # 99% complete in <5s
claims_saga_duration_seconds_bucket{saga_type="claims-processing",le="+Inf"} 10000

# Saga success rate
claims_saga_success_rate{saga_type="claims-processing"} 0.9987  # 99.87% success rate

# Compensation rate by failure reason
claims_saga_compensation_rate{saga_type="claims-processing",reason="eligibility-check-failed"} 0.0005
claims_saga_compensation_rate{saga_type="claims-processing",reason="prior-auth-missing"} 0.0008
claims_saga_compensation_rate{saga_type="claims-processing",reason="payment-service-timeout"} 0.0002
```

